<title>NORWAY: Norske Skog drops merger talks with Moelven.</title>
<headline>Norske Skog drops merger talks with Moelven.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian forestry group Norske Skog ASA said on Monday it had dropped talks with Moelven Industrier ASA on merging their units for saw mills and board production.  </p>
<p>&quot;These talks have now ended without the parties coming to agreement,&quot; Norske Skog said in a statement to the Oslo Bourse.</p>
<p>The companies announced on April 25 they had started a discussion on the subject because they agreed on the need for a restructuring of this sector in Norway.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
